==Strategies==
If you wish to convert, use the Community Divination Training server (world 79). If you wish to subdue, use any low-population world.

For players who prefer to convert, it is possible to use the [[Surge]] ability to move faster between the [[Unstable rift (Guthixian Cache)|unstable rift]] and memory deposits. If the player has access to the [[Invention]] skill, consider augmenting a piece of body or leg armour (weapons are not suitable due to needing empty hands for the minigame) and add the [[Mobile]] [[perk]] to it. It costs no energy to use, and cuts Surge / Escape's cooldown by half. [[Dive]] can be used in conjunction with [[Surge]], allowing players to quickly move to and from the memory and rift at breakneck speeds.

Being in a stream of other players helps evade active automatons as they can only target one player at a time, reducing the chances of being attacked compared to running alone.

If there are not many other players during a cache, it is usually faster points to subdue as many automatons as possible rather than converting memories. This is especially true for players lacking Divination levels for high-tier memories (for subduing, most Automatons are Ancient and can be subdued with 1 Divination). This could also be considered if there is an abundance of active automatons. Try to change forms in turns with other players to maximise the points of subduing automatons.

The double points ability is best utilised in human form by carrying a memory to the rift, activating the ability immediately before depositing, then running back, allowing players to get 2 memories per ability activation (with the [[Mobile]] [[perk]], 3 memories per activation are possible). In Cres' form, it is best used when an Enraged automaton is about to reactivate and there are no other players nearby.

Just before transforming from Cres' form back to human form, if the "subdue all automatons" ability is available, use it so that you can quickly deposit memories in human form without automatons' interference. 

==Rewards==
Rewards include [[Divination]] experience, three temporary passive benefits, and an outfit.

===Experience===
The [[experience]] reward is given according to level and the amount of points obtained during the cache. The game can be played as many times as desired. However, the points in one cache is capped at 100. Players can determine how much experience they will earn by hovering the cursor over the points. Exiting the cache early will still award experience relative to the points you've earned.

The experience rewarded is not boostable.

{{Chart data|Chart data/guthixian cache|width=40vw|height=40vh}}

===Benefits===
[[File:Converting all memories.gif|160px|thumb|One of the temporary rewards for completing a cache]]
* 10% chance for double loot from [[divine location]]s, at no extra cost to the player's gathering limit. Upon occurring, the player gets the message: {{RSFont|color=#36a51b|You received double loot, as you recently completed a Guthix cache!}}
** Does not activate for [[divine simulacrum]]s.
**If players have the "Shared Knowledge" perk from [[Memorial to Guthix]] active, they will instead receive 25% extra experience for each double loot activation instead of items.
* 10% chance to save a charge from a [[sign of the porter]]. Upon occurring, the player gets the message: {{RSFont|color=#36a51b|As you completed a Guthixian cache recently, your sign of the porter did not lose a charge.}}
*10% chance to convert all memories at once while training Divination, this can happen with all the options (energy, enhanced experience and normal experience), and still consumes the normal amount of energy for enhanced experience. Upon occurring, you get a unique animation.
These last for <math>\frac{points}{20}</math> minutes, up to a maximum of 5 minutes. The timer for these will continue to deplete when logged out and will appear as this icon: [[File:Guthix cache boosts (self status).png]]

Players with the Stored Power perk from [[Memorial to Guthix]] will instead receive a [[Guthixian cache boost (small)]] when completing a Guthixian cache with 100 points. This allows the player to use the boost later at their convenience, rather than immediately upon exiting the cache. 

If players lack inventory space, you will not get bonus loot: {{RSFont|color=#fe8b37|You would have received double loot due to recently completing a Guthixian Cache. However, you did not have enough space.}}

===Diviner's outfit===
If the player doesn't own the full [[diviner's outfit]] [[Skilling outfits|skilling outfit]] set, there is a chance they will receive a part they don't own upon completing a cache (including [[Ironman Mode|ironmen]]). The chance of receiving a piece is 0.5% per point that the player scores within the cache (50% at 100 points, 40% at 80 points, etc.). You have to score at least one point to have a chance at earning an outfit piece. Pieces can only be obtained if the player receives experience from the cache.{{CiteForum|url=http://services.runescape.com/m=forum/forums.ws?74,75,52,65949497,goto,21#205|author=Mod Timbo|postdate=17 November 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/11779832|archivedate=18 November 2017|title=Dev Blog: Revealing Drop Rates|forum=Existing Game Content}}
When an outfit piece is received, you get the message: {{RSFont|color=#00db00|As a reward for your dedication, the Guthixian guardians award you with a piece of the Diviner's outfit.}}

